## FVWMTABS_DIR is set by the FvwmTabs module from its actual ModulePath.
## Example: ModulePath ${HOME}/.fvwm/modules:+
##
## Commands reach the FvwmTabs server through FvwmMFL.:
## each function runs `Echo FvwmTabsCmd <command>`. FVWM broadcasts that as an
## MX_ECHO packet, FvwmMFL re-emits it as an "echo" event on its socket, and the
## FvwmTabs server (subscribed to "echo") strips the FvwmTabsCmd tag and runs.
##
## Load FvwmMFL before FvwmTabs in StartFunction.

## Create new tabber

DestroyFunc NewTabber
AddToFunc NewTabber
+ I Echo FvwmTabsCmd createNewTabber $*

## Legacy/default tabber commands.

DestroyFunc Tabize
AddToFunc Tabize
+ I Function FvwmTabs_TabizeLoop $[FVWMTABS_DEFAULT_ID]

DestroyFunc TabizeActive
AddToFunc TabizeActive
+ I Echo FvwmTabsCmd tabizeActive

DestroyFunc TabizeTo
AddToFunc TabizeTo
+ I Function FvwmTabs_TabizeLoop $0

DestroyFunc DestroyTabber
AddToFunc DestroyTabber
+ I Echo FvwmTabsCmd destroyTabber $[FVWMTABS_DEFAULT_ID]

DestroyFunc DestroyActiveTabber
AddToFunc DestroyActiveTabber
+ I Echo FvwmTabsCmd destroyActiveTabber

DestroyFunc DestroyTabberId
AddToFunc DestroyTabberId
+ I Echo FvwmTabsCmd destroyTabber $0

DestroyFunc NextTab
AddToFunc NextTab
+ I Echo FvwmTabsCmd nextTab $[FVWMTABS_DEFAULT_ID]

DestroyFunc NextTabActive
AddToFunc NextTabActive
+ I Echo FvwmTabsCmd nextTabActive

DestroyFunc NextTabId
AddToFunc NextTabId
+ I Echo FvwmTabsCmd nextTab $0

DestroyFunc PrevTab
AddToFunc PrevTab
+ I Echo FvwmTabsCmd prevTab $[FVWMTABS_DEFAULT_ID]

DestroyFunc PrevTabActive
AddToFunc PrevTabActive
+ I Echo FvwmTabsCmd prevTabActive

DestroyFunc PrevTabId
AddToFunc PrevTabId
+ I Echo FvwmTabsCmd prevTab $0

## Change a tabber's numeric ID. "Renaming" here means reassigning the ID
## number, not setting a free-text label. The request is refused (an error
## dialog appears, nothing changes) if NEW_ID is already used by another
## tabber, so two tabbers can never share an ID.

DestroyFunc ChangeTabberId
AddToFunc ChangeTabberId
+ I Echo FvwmTabsCmd changeTabberId $0 $1

DestroyFunc ChangeActiveTabberId
AddToFunc ChangeActiveTabberId
+ I Echo FvwmTabsCmd changeActiveTabberId $0

DestroyFunc QuitFvwmTabs
AddToFunc QuitFvwmTabs
+ I Echo FvwmTabsCmd quit

## Root menu (right-click):

DestroyMenu TabbersMenu
AddToMenu TabbersMenu "FvwmTabs" Title
+ "Create New Tabber" Function NewTabber
+ "Add Window(s)" Function TabizeActive
+ "" Nop
+ "Next Tab" Function NextTabActive
+ "Previous Tab" Function PrevTabActive
+ "" Nop
+ "Destroy Tabber" Function DestroyActiveTabber

## Optional key bindings (users may comment out)

Key T A CM Function NewTabber
Key W A CM Function Tabize
Key Right A CM Function NextTab
Key Left A CM Function PrevTab

## Optional root-window menu binding (comment out in FvwmTabs.conf if you already use a right-click root menu).
## Example: Mouse 3 R A Menu TabbersMenu mouse 0p 0p

Read $[FVWMTABS_DIR]/FvwmTabs.conf
